<title>UK: Orange shares up on talk of Natwest upgrade.</title>
<headline>Orange shares up on talk of Natwest upgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Orange Plc climbed on Wednesday amid market talk that analysts at NatWest Securities had upgraded their recommendation on the stock.</p>
<p>Market-makers said NatWest was believed to have issued a research document on the telecommunications sector which included upgraded recommendations on Orange and British Telecommunications Plc.</p>
<p>By 0851 GMT Orange shares were 5-1/2p higher at 216 while BT was 2-1/2p firmer at 441.</p>
<p>Analysts at NatWest declined to comment.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
